; Tutorial_8_Use_the_Catalog_in_DbDo_and_Stay_Current.inix -- use the catalog in dbdo and stay current

[about]
Title=8 - Use the Catalog in DbDo and Stay Current
Intro=The catalog as a database you can browse and search in DbDo, the workbook, and keeping everything current with later runs.
Setup=DbDo installed, and a catalog gathered.
Homework=Open bookFido's database in DbDo, filter it by one author, and say how many books you have by that author.

[step]

Say=One want: to ask my whole collection questions, such as every book by one author, or everything published before 1950.
Key=

[step]

Say=Besides the documents, bookFido keeps bookFido dot d b, a database in DbDo's standard shape, in its data folder.
Key=

[step]

Say=It holds books, authors and publishers as related tables, so each author is one record with all their books beneath it.
Key=

[step]

Say=I open it in DbDo with Control plus O.
Key=Control+O
Hear=Open Database dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The books table opens first.
Key=
Hear=books, 450 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus F, then the first choice, Any field, finds a word wherever it is: an author's surname, a series, a reader of the book.
Key=Control+F
Hear=Filter Records dialog
Hear=Filter by: list box, Any field contains text
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Enter, I type Tolkien, and Enter again.
Key=Enter
Hear=12 records have Tolkien.
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus Right Arrow goes from a book to its author's record, and from an author to all of their books.
Key=Alt+Right Arrow
Hear=authors, 1 record
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The workbook, bookFido dot x l s x, has a sheet for each library, for anyone who prefers a spreadsheet.
Key=

[step]

Say=Keeping current is a matter of running bookFido again, weekly or monthly, with sign ins remembered by its own browser profile.
Key=

[step]

Say=If a run is interrupted, the next continues where it stopped, from the progress saved every couple of minutes.
Key=

[step]

Say=The documents in Downloads are rewritten each time, so the copy you open is always the latest.
Key=

[step]

Say=In DbDo, Control plus G goes to a record by number, and Shift plus Y says how many records are in view, the same keys as any DbDo database.
Key=Shift+Y
Hear=12 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Control plus Shift plus F clears the filter, and the whole collection is back.
Key=Control+Shift+F
Hear=books, 450 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Alt plus O orders the books by any column, such as year, oldest first, for a look at the collection by age.
Key=Alt+O
Hear=Order Records dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=The database is rewritten by each run, so DbDo shows the latest gathering when it is next opened.
Key=

[step]

Say=For a spreadsheet user, the workbook's sheets carry a bold header row that the screen reader announces with each cell.
Key=

[step]

Say=Inside DbDo, Shift plus F12 asks the model on your own computer a question about the table, such as which authors you read most.
Key=Shift+F12
Hear=Chat about Table dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Escape closes it, unasked, and the table is as it was.
Key=Escape
Hear=books, 450 records
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=And Alt plus X exports the books in view, after a filter, to a spreadsheet or a document of their own.
Key=Alt+X
Hear=Export Data dialog
Note=Confirm the wording with a live run: buildTutorials -live.

[step]

Say=Questions in DbDo, documents in the browser, a workbook for sorting: one collection, three ways in. The last walk gathers it all.
Key=
